        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hume Auctioneers - We Get The Pick Of The Crop.\n\nOverlooking an attractive greenspace in the highly regarded Fairgreen development, this beautiful detached residence offers spacious, well-proportioned accommodation and a superb family-friendly layout.\n\nPresented in excellent condition throughout, this bright and inviting home is ideally located within walking distance of schools, shops, leisure facilities and Portlaoise town centre, while also enjoying easy access to the M7 motorway.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, a generous front living room with feature fireplace and large windows flooding the room with natural light, and a spacious open-plan kitchen/dining room stretching the full depth of the property. The kitchen offers an excellent range of fitted units and ample dining space with direct access to the rear garden. Off the kitchen is a practical utility room together with a guest bathroom. There is also a large walk in pantry storage press.\n\nUpstairs, the property boasts four well-proportioned bedrooms, including a master bedroom with ensuite shower room. A fully tiled family bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation.\n\nOutside, the property enjoys a private rear garden with lawn, patio area and a detached high quality outside room which is fully insulated and wired, providing excellent storage or potential for a home office, gym or hobby space. To the front, there is off-street parking and an attractive low-maintenance exterior. \n\nSuch is the quality of this home, it has been awarded a B3 energy rating, meaning not alone will your heating bills be minimised, the property also qualifies for a super low-interest rate green mortgage.\n\nThe property has an EV charging point installed.\n\nThis is an ideal family home in a mature and established neighbourhood, offering excellent space, privacy and convenience.\n\nFairgreen is exceptionally convenient. Within walking distance of schools, train station, town centre and restaurants, everything is at hand.\n\n And now with the recent opening of Tesco express within the development, the location has got even better. \n\nFibre broadband to the door. Gas central heating. \n\nViewing of this exceptional home is highly recommended. \n\nThe new Portlaoise Bus service has a stop 1 minute walk from the property, giving round the clock access to Hospital, Train Station, Town Centre and Schools.\n"
